From 520b06e920a21e0f5908f3c3b550ec35e292c309 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 18:54:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 087/114] rust: drm: add typed RAII event channels

Add event delivery for a concrete DRM driver and file pair. A connection
token owns the logical receiver and disconnects automatically on drop.

Reserve a private pending-event anchor for each connection. DRM
core clears its file pointer under event_lock during close, so send
can test and queue under the same lock without retaining an erased
or dangling drm_file pointer. Validate the event payload layout at
compile time and bind each channel to its exact DRM device.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
---
